\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. To the haven of Thy breast,
\par O Son of Man, I fly;
\par Be my refuge and my rest,
\par For O the storm is high!
\par Save me from the furious blast,
\par A covert from the tempest be;
\par Hide me, Jesus, till o'erpast
\par The storm of sin I see.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Welcome as the water- spring
\par To a dry, barren place,
\par O descend on me, and bring
\par Thy sweet refreshing grace!
\par O'er a parched and weary land
\par As a great rock extends its shade,
\par Hide me, Saviour, with Thine hand,
\par And screen my naked head.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. In the time of my distress
\par Thou hast my succour been,
\par In my utter helplessness
\par Restraining me from sin;
\par O how swiftly didst Thou move
\par To save me in the trying hour!
\par Still protect me with Thy love,
\par And shield me with Thy power.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. First and last in me perform
\par The work Thou hast begun;
\par Be my shelter from the storm,
\par My shadow from the sun;
\par Weary, parched with thirst, and faint,
\par Till Thou the abiding Spirit breathe,
\par Every moment, Lord, I want
\par The merit of Thy death.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

